 "datePublished": "2012?",
 "description": "The more I read on Emperor Tewodros the more difficult it became to present his story in a simplified way to the younger generation of Ethiopia. Most books on Tewodros depict him as a barbarian and a cruel man. He was a character who lived in turbulent times. He was a victim of circumstances and did what he did when he was pushed. Especially the poor knew him for his generosity. He was a man of vision and sincerely wanted to modernize Ethiopia",
